{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"mutating","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"reconcile","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"with","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"remote","kind":"internalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"EntityStore","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore","preciseIdentifier":"s:6Swidux11EntityStoreV"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Entity","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"deleting","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"deletedIDs","kind":"internalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Set","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sh"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"UUID","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:10Foundation4UUIDV"},{"text":">, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"preserving","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Set","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sh"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"UUID","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:10Foundation4UUIDV"},{"text":">)","kind":"text"}],"platforms":["macOS"]}]},{"kind":"parameters","parameters":[{"name":"remote","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The rows read from storage for the IDs in question. Rows for","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"IDs the caller didn’t ask about are simply not here, and their","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"absence means nothing.","type":"text"}]}]},{"name":"deletedIDs","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"IDs storage reports as deleted elsewhere. Removed with","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the same origin a full reconcile uses, so no deletion is recorded and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"none is echoed back to the store it came from. An ID that "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"remote"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"still holds is "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"not","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" removed however it is named here: a live row"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is positive evidence, and a tombstone can be stale.","type":"text"}]}]},{"name":"preserving","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"IDs the caller knows carry unflushed local intent, exactly"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"as in the full reconcile. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"remote"},{"text":" has no authority over them, and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"neither does ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"deletedIDs"},{"text":". This store’s own un-drained ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore\/changes","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" are"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"folded in automatically."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"discussion","level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Discussion"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The counterpart to "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore\/reconcile(with:preserving:removingMissing:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" for a","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"partial read — a refresh of the rows a sync tick reported as changed,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"rather than of the whole table. Absorbing rows works identically; what"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"changes is where deletions come from."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A partial snapshot "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"cannot","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" infer deletion from absence. An ID missing"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"from it was not deleted, it was not asked for, and treating the two alike"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"would empty the store on the first partial merge. So removal is driven","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"entirely by ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"deletedIDs"},{"text":", which the caller must have positive evidence","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"for — a history tombstone, not an empty result."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Does ","type":"text"},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"not","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" record changes — this is a hydration operation, for the same"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"reason the full reconcile isn’t one.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore\/reconcile(with:deleting:preserving:)"},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Reconciles this store against a snapshot covering only "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"some","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" of its IDs.","type":"text"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore"]]},"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/swidux\/entitystore\/reconcile(with:deleting:preserving:)"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"metadata":{"externalID":"s:6Swidux11EntityStoreV9reconcile4with8deleting10preservingyACyxG_Shy10Foundation4UUIDVGALtF","symbolKind":"method","title":"reconcile(with:deleting:preserving:)","roleHeading":"Instance Method","role":"symbol","modules":[{"name":"Swidux"}],"fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"reconcile","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"with","kind"